    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are prioritizing high-upside matchups today, led by **Kyle Tucker** (78.26) and **Andy Pages** (69.49). **Kyle Tucker** is our premier play against Randy V\u00e1squez, as the favorable 4.76 xERA matchup and his elite projected efficiency make him a locked-in core starter. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (68.58) earns a high score despite facing the difficult Roki Sasaki; his efficiency is bolstered by a significant +13% boost from his dynamic platoon splits and a +2% edge due to Sasaki\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-probability environment for **Jackson Merrill** to secure the stolen bases we desperately need. **Sam Antonacci** (65.19) also rounds out the top tier, benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against Slade Cecconi and a premium spot at the top of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nolan Schanuel** (39.17), who narrowly missed the starting lineup. While **Nolan Schanuel** projects reasonably well, the optimizer prioritized the aggressive platoon and order advantages of **Liam Hicks** (57.75) and **Dominic Smith** (48.09) in their respective slots. **Josh Lowe** (45.01) remains a high-risk start; while his raw score is bolstered by his dynamic platoon edge (+14%), he is facing an elite arm in Bryce Miller (2.42 xERA) in a park that penalizes his output by 5%. We are monitoring the status of **Jordan Westburg** closely, as his continued presence on the IL forces our bench depth to carry more weight than ideal. Owners should keep a close watch on the official lineups, as the current projections for **Drake Baldwin** and **Miguel Vargas** are predicated on assumed spots at the top of their respective orders; any downward movement in the lineup will necessitate a swift re-evaluation of their daily value.",
